  "text": "Allergies:\nCodeine / Ultram / Beta-Blockers (Beta-Adrenergic Blocking Agts) \n/ Flagyl / Oxycodone\n\nChief Complaint:\nleft cheek defect\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ female with a history of having Mohs procedure for \ncutaneous malignancy of left medial cheek area.  This is in over \nan area of 5 x 4 cm and she presents for staged reconstruction \nand incidentally, she also has a history of possible DVT in the \npast.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nMs. ___ was admitted to the plastic surgery service \nfollowing a left cervicofacial rotational advancement and STSG \nto defect, tie over bolster. She was stable during her \npost-operative stay. She was given analgesics for pain, \nantiemetics for nausea, and antibiotics. She was able to \nambulate. Diet was advanced. She was discharged home with ___ \nservices and on antibiotics on post op day 1\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nleft cheek and nasal defect",
